---
import Journey from '../../layouts/Journey.astro';
import Step from '../../components/journey/Step.astro';
import More from '../../components/journey/More.astro';
import Next from '../../components/journey/Next.astro';
import ForLevel from '../../components/level/ForLevel.astro';
import CopyPrompt from '../../components/site/CopyPrompt.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/nav';
---
<Journey chapter="people" first="pr" title="Other people" description="Agents write the change; people decide what gets built and whether it ships. Pull requests, a colleague's review, clients and users.">
  <Step id="pr" title="A pull request waits for a person">
    <p>Agents write the change; people decide what gets built and whether it ships. A pull request is the agent’s branch stopped in front of main, with <a href={url('journey/check/')}>the check</a> run on it and <a href={url('journey/proof/')}>its proof</a> beside it, until a person says yes.</p>
    <ForLevel is={['technical', 'engineer']}><p>The check here is CI: the type check and the tests run on every push to the branch, and main only takes a branch that passed.</p></ForLevel>
    <More title="A prompt for this">
      <CopyPrompt compact title="Write the pull request for a person">Open a pull request for this change, written for someone who has not seen this thread:
1. What changed and why, in three lines.
2. How you checked it: the commands you ran and what they printed, and screenshots of anything visible.
3. What to look at first, by file.
4. What you did not check.</CopyPrompt>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="peer" title="A colleague has to read it">
    <p>Ten agents, one colleague, a made-up day: the readout counts what landed and what still waits. Big changes with no proof pile up at the check; small ones with proof go through.</p>
    <ForLevel is="engineer"><p>Review time is the queue’s service time. Smaller diffs with evidence shorten it; more agents only lengthen the queue.</p></ForLevel>
    <div class="pick" role="group" aria-label="What reaches the colleague">
      <button type="button" data-do="size" data-val="big" data-default aria-pressed="true">Big, no proof</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="size" data-val="proof" aria-pressed="false">Big, with proof</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="size" data-val="small" aria-pressed="false">Small, with proof</button>
    </div>
  </Step>
  <Step id="client" title="A client tries the thing, not the code">
    <p>Send a client a link to a running copy of the change. What they ask for comes back to you and becomes the agent’s next brief.</p>
    <ForLevel is={['technical', 'engineer']}><p>Most hosts can build a preview link for every pull request; ask the agent to set it up once.</p></ForLevel>
    <div class="pick" role="group" aria-label="What the client gets">
      <button type="button" data-do="link" data-val="link" data-default aria-pressed="true">A link to try</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="link" data-val="code" aria-pressed="false">The code</button>
    </div>
  </Step>
  <Step id="users" title="Users find what nobody tested">
    <p>Hand a user’s report to the agent as the brief, and ask for a test with the fix. Then the check knows that mistake if it ever comes back.</p>
    <div class="pick" role="group" aria-label="How the fix lands">
      <button type="button" data-do="test" data-val="with" data-default aria-pressed="true">Fix with a test</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="test" data-val="without" aria-pressed="false">Fix without</button>
    </div>
    <More title="A prompt for this">
      <CopyPrompt compact title="A fix from a user's report">A user reported this: [paste what they saw]. First write a test that fails because of it and show me it fails. Then fix it, and show me the test passing and the rest of the tests still passing.</CopyPrompt>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="loop" title="The widest loop">
    <p>After the first release most briefs come from a colleague, a client or a user. You pass them on and read what comes back.</p>
    <div class="row">
      <button class="btn ghost" type="button" data-do="again">Run it again</button>
    </div>
    <Next from="people" more={[{ href: 'wiki/pull-request/', text: 'Pull requests', side: true }, { href: 'wiki/review/', text: 'Reviewing a change', side: true }]} />
  </Step>
  <Fragment slot="foot">
    <p>The day, the rates and what people say are made up to show the mechanism.</p>
  </Fragment>
</Journey>
